── GATE SWEEP (loosen each gate one notch -> fwd return of the names it NEWLY admits) ──
  positive = the gate was too tight (newly-admitted beat the field); ≤0 = it's keeping junk out.
  the TOO TIGHT flag needs mean AND median positive — one survivor can carry a mean on its own.
  vs shipped = newly-admitted median MINUS the accepted cohort's median (-49.9); >0 = no worse than what the gates already keep.
  growth_min_range_pct -10   admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_cagr -4         n=15   fwd peer-relative  mean -24.5 | med -79.9 pts  vs shipped -30.0
  growth_min_1y_pct -10      n=4    fwd peer-relative  mean +1.3 | med -72.2 pts  vs shipped -22.3  <- SPLIT (tail-driven, read the median)
  max_1m_drop_pct -10 (deeper) admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  min_avg_turnover_eur ->0   admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_max_above_ma ->off  n=10   fwd peer-relative  mean -74.2 | med -81.8 pts  vs shipped -31.9
  growth_require_lifetime_uptrend ->off admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_maxdd_cap ->off     admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_leg_years ->2 (admits the 2Y rung) n=10   fwd peer-relative  mean +4.6 | med +16.3 pts  vs shipped +66.2  <- ADMITS NO WORSE THAN THE BOOK  <- TOO TIGHT (loosen this gate)
